Issue: Bun's CSS loader fails to properly flatten nested @layer rules, causing malformed CSS output.
Example: When using Tailwind CSS v4 with DaisyUI, input fields only render one rounded corner instead of four. Inspecting the CSS shows all border-radius properties incorrectly target border-top-left-radius:
.input {
  border-top-left-radius: var(--radius-field);
  border-top-left-radius: var(--radius-field);
  border-top-left-radius: var(--radius-field);
  border-top-left-radius: var(--radius-field);
}
Root cause: The bug occurs when using loader: "css" in Bun plugins. Using loader: "js" to inject CSS as a <style> tag works correctly.
Minimal reproduction: https://github.com/daggamault/bun-css-loader-bug
Note: This is not specific to DaisyUI—any library using nested @layer rules will be affected. The same code works correctly in Next.js.

