node test.cjs
What is the expected behavior?
Each message should be delivered once per messaging system. Node.js output:
Handler 1: 1
Result: 1

What do you see instead?
Both handlers fire for each message. Bun output:
Handler 1: 1
Handler 2: 2
Result: 2

Additional information
It appears parentPort.on('message', ...) is internally implemented using self.addEventListener('message', ...). When code registers handlers for both Node.js worker_threads (parentPort.on) and Web Workers (self.onmessage), each message is delivered twice.
This breaks Emscripten-compiled WASM modules which commonly register handlers for both environments to support Node.js and browsers:
// For Node.js worker_threads:
parentPort.on('message', (msg) => onmessage({ data: msg }));

// For Web Workers:
self.onmessage = handleMessage;
In Node.js, self is undefined in worker_threads, so only the parentPort handler runs. In browsers, parentPort is undefined, so only self.onmessage runs. In Bun, both exist and both fire.
This affects z3-solver and likely other Emscripten-compiled packages: #19453

