What is the type of issue?
Documentation is missing
What is the issue?
When calling socket.upgradeTLS() with a new socket handler, the original (non-TLS) socket handler still remain active and continue receiving events (data, drain, close, etc) until socket is closed.
Additionally, the original socket handler receives TLS handshake / encrypted bytes in data() during/after the upgrade, while the new TLS handler receives decrypted plaintext.
This is surprising behavior, and it’s unclear whether it is intended or a bug.
const textDecoder = new TextDecoder();
const textEncoder = new TextEncoder();

// Initial plain socket connection and socket handler
const socket = await Bun.connect({
  hostname: "ip.me",
  port: 443,
  socket: {
    data(socket, data) {
      console.log("NON-TLS received data:", textDecoder.decode(data));
    },
    drain(socket) {
      console.log("NON-TLS socket drained");
    },
    close(socket, error) {
      console.log("NON-TLS socket closed", error ?? "");
    },
  },
});

// Upgrade to TLS with a new socket handler
socket.upgradeTLS({
  tls: true,
  socket: {
    data(socket, data) {
      console.log("TLS received data:", textDecoder.decode(data));
    },
    drain(socket) {
      console.log("TLS socket drained");
    },
    close(socket, error) {
      console.log("TLS socket closed", error ?? "");
    },
    handshake(socket, success, authorizationError) {
      if (!success) {
        console.error("TLS handshake failed:", authorizationError);
        process.exit(1);
      }

      socket.write(
        textEncoder.encode(
          "GET / HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: ip.me\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n",
        ),
      );
    },
  },
});

TLS upgrade started: TLS handshake bytes are delivered to the original (non-TLS) socket.data() handler.

After TLS handshake completes: both original and TLS socket handlers continue receiving events (data/drain/close/...). TLS handler receives decrypted HTTP response.

Where did you find it?
TCPSocket.upgradeTLS
I found this while implementing my own protocol that does STARTTLS / PostgreSQL-style TLS-upgrade.
