133

Additional information

This is macOS-specific (Apple Silicon M3)
The crash occurs specifically when using the "utf-8" encoding parameter
Reading as a Buffer (fs.readFileSync(path) without encoding) may behave differently
Related to #2570 (String and JSON size limits) but this is a crash rather than truncation
Similar to #17941 but that was Windows-specific and fixed by #21738

The root cause appears to be a missing bounds check before attempting to create a JavaScript string that exceeds the engine's string length limit. Node.js checks the size and throws ERR_STRING_TOO_LONG, while Bun attempts the allocation and triggers SIGTRAP.

