  ...define  // <-- This can contain undefined values
};
When a user sets process.env.VITE_* to JSON.stringify(undefined) (which returns undefined, not the string "undefined"), this undefined value flows through to rolldown's Rust bindings.
Node.js's N-API handles undefined leniently, but Bun's N-API strictly requires the expected type (String), causing the build to fail.

