Description
WebSocket messages sent immediately after the handshake (in the server's open callback) are not queued if the onmessage handler is not set at the time of message arrival. This differs from browser WebSocket behavior where early messages are queued until a handler is attached.
Environment

Bun Version: Latest (tested on 1.3.6)
Platform: Linux
Reproduction: See test cases below

Expected Behavior
In browser WebSocket implementations (Chrome, Firefox, etc.), messages sent by the server immediately after the handshake are queued internally and delivered to the onmessage handler once it is set, even if set milliseconds later.
Actual Behavior
In Bun's WebSocket client, messages sent before the onmessage handler is attached are discarded/lost.
Test Cases
I've created comprehensive tests demonstrating this behavior:
Test 1: Message Loss with Delayed onmessage After WebSocket Creation
// WebSocket created, 50ms delay, then onmessage set, then onopen set
const ws = new WebSocket(wsUrl);
await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 50)); // Connection starts
ws.onmessage = (event) => { /* handle */ }; // Set after messages sent
ws.onopen = () => { /* handle */ };
// Result: 0 messages received
Test 2: Message Loss with onmessage Set After onopen
ws.onopen = () => {
  setTimeout(() => {
    ws.onmessage = (event) => { /* handle */ }; // Set after onopen
  }, 50);
};
// Result: 0 messages received
Test 3: Safe Pattern - Messages Received
const ws = new WebSocket(wsUrl);
ws.onmessage = (event) => { /* handle */ }; // Set immediately
ws.onopen = () => { /* handle */ };
// Result: All early messages received
Impact

Code expecting browser WebSocket behavior may lose messages
Timing-sensitive WebSocket applications may fail unexpectedly
Migration from browser/Node to Bun requires handler timing changes

Reproduction Steps

Run the attached test file in a Bun environment
Observe that tests expecting message loss pass (0 messages received)
Compare with browser behavior where messages would be queued

Suggested Fix
Align Bun's WebSocket client with browser behavior by queuing early messages until onmessage is set.
Related Issues

#7525: onmessage receives raw data instead of MessageEvent
#4529: WebSocket header casing differences

