What steps can reproduce the bug?
When dependabot runs bun update @some/package, the root dependency gets re-resolved to va.b.d, but @some/other's transitive dep on @some/package^a.0.0 keeps its old resolution (va.b.c). Both versions end up in the lockfile even though va.b.d satisfies all ranges. This happens because the Cloner in cleanWithLogger carries forward old resolutions without checking if a newer compatible version already exists.
What is the expected behavior?
Transitive deps should be updated and @some/other's transitive dep on @some/package^a.0.0 should be resolved to va.b.d as well.
What do you see instead?
@some/other's transitive dep on @some/package^a.0.0 keeps its old resolution (va.b.c).
Additional information
Probable Root Cause
In src/install/lockfile/Package.zig:190-205, during Package.clone():
 for (old_resolutions, resolutions, 0..) |old_resolution, *resolution, i| {
     const mapped = package_id_mapping[old_resolution];
     if (mapped < max_package_id) {
         resolution.* = mapped;           // Uses mapped ID, never checks for better version
     } else {
         try cloner.clone_queue.append(…); // Queues old package for cloning, never checks if compatible version exists
     }
 }
And in src/install/lockfile.zig:869-886 (Cloner.flush()):
 while (this.clone_queue.pop()) |to_clone| {
     const mapping = this.mapping[to_clone.old_resolution];
     if (mapping < max_package_id) {
         this.lockfile.buffers.resolutions.items[to_clone.resolve_id] = mapping; // Same: no better-version check
         continue;
     }
     // Clones old package unconditionally
 }
Neither location checks whether a newer compatible version already exists in the new lockfile.
