Root cause analysis
StatWatcher in src/bun.js/node/node_fs_stat_watcher.zig has a thread-safety bug:

StatWatcher uses ThreadSafeRefCount, so deref() can be called from any thread
It has last_jsvalue: jsc.Strong.Optional -- a HandleSet-backed strong GC handle
finalize() (line 352) does NOT call close(). It only sets closed = true and calls deref()
close() (line 337) safely clears last_jsvalue via clearWithoutDeallocation(), but finalize() skips this step

The race:

GC calls finalize() on the JS thread: sets closed=true, calls deref() (refcount 2->1)
StatWatcherScheduler.workPoolCallback() (line 126) runs on a WorkPool thread: sees closed==true at line 140, calls watcher.deref() at line 141 (refcount 1->0)
deinit() runs on the WorkPool thread (line 236): calls this.last_jsvalue.deinit() (line 247)
This calls Bun__StrongRef__delete -> HandleSet::deallocate() from a non-JS thread
HandleSet::deallocate() modifies HandleSet::m_strongList (an intrusive linked list) without synchronization
