Bug
getColorDepth() returns 8 (256-color) inside tmux even when COLORTERM=truecolor is set, because the TMUX environment variable check short-circuits before COLORTERM is evaluated.
This affects both:

Zig native: src/output.zig line 287 (TMUX check) vs line 315 (COLORTERM check)
JS polyfill: src/js/internal/tty.ts line 108 (TMUX check) vs line 144 (COLORTERM check)

tmux has supported true color since v2.2 (2016). Modern tmux sets COLORTERM=truecolor when the outer terminal supports RGB. The current ordering ignores this and always caps tmux sessions at 256 colors.
Reproduction
// color-mre.js — run inside a tmux session with COLORTERM=truecolor
const tty = require('tty');
console.log('TMUX:', process.env.TMUX || '(unset)');
console.log('COLORTERM:', process.env.COLORTERM || '(unset)');
console.log('getColorDepth():', process.stdout.getColorDepth());
console.log('hasColors(16777216):', process.stdout.hasColors(16777216));
Inside tmux (with COLORTERM=truecolor):
TMUX: /private/tmp/tmux-501/default,9842,1
COLORTERM: truecolor
getColorDepth(): 8          # ← wrong, should be 24
hasColors(16777216): false   # ← wrong, should be true

Outside tmux:
TMUX: (unset)
COLORTERM: truecolor
getColorDepth(): 24          # ← correct
hasColors(16777216): true     # ← correct

Workaround (TMUX=):
TMUX: (unset)
COLORTERM: truecolor
getColorDepth(): 24          # ← correct
hasColors(16777216): true     # ← correct

Real-world impact
This causes applications built with Bun (e.g. Claude Code) to emit 256-color escape sequences (\e[38;5;Nm) instead of true color (\e[38;2;R;G;Bm) when running inside tmux, producing visibly incorrect colors.
Suggested fix
Move the COLORTERM truecolor/24bit check before the TMUX check in both locations:
src/output.zig — move lines 315-319 before line 287:
// Check COLORTERM first — tmux sets this when RGB is supported
if (bun.env_var.COLORTERM.get()) |color_term| {
    if (strings.eqlComptime(color_term, "truecolor") or strings.eqlComptime(color_term, "24bit")) {
        lazy_color_depth = .@"16m";
        return;
    }
}

if (bun.env_var.TMUX.get() != null) {
    lazy_color_depth = .@"256";
    return;
}
src/js/internal/tty.ts — same reordering at lines 108/144.
