import dns from "dns";
dns.lookup("localhost", { all: true }, (err, addresses) => {
  console.log(addresses);
  // [ { address: '::1', family: 6 }, { address: '127.0.0.1', family: 4 } ]
});
::1 is returned first. Docker binds to 0.0.0.0 (IPv4 only), so the IPv6 attempt hangs.
Node.js solves this with autoSelectFamily: true (default since v20) in net.createConnection(), which implements Happy Eyeballs at the socket API level — meaning all libraries automatically benefit.
Bun's Happy Eyeballs (PR #11206) only covers Bun-native APIs (fetch, Bun.connect), not the Node.js net compatibility layer that third-party libraries use.
