What is the expected behavior?
File descriptor count should stay stable. Serving 304 Not Modified or HEAD responses on static file routes should not leak file descriptors.
What do you see instead?
Every 304 and HEAD response leaks exactly one file descriptor. 400 requests = 400 leaked fds. Under production CDN traffic this would exhaust the OS fd limit within minutes/hours, causing EMFILE: too many open files.
Additional information
Root cause: FileRoute.zig:on() opens an fd at line 187, but only transfers ownership to StreamTransfer at line 271. Four early-return paths between those lines skip the transfer without closing the fd:
Line 189: catch return on dateForHeader()
Line 230: catch return on lastModifiedDate()
Lines 252-256: Status codes 204/205/304/307/308 (bodiless responses)
Lines 265-268: HEAD method
The fix is to add bun.Async.Closer.close(fd, ...) on each path, matching the existing pattern on line 218 (!can_serve_file case).

