What is the expected behavior?
agent.maxSockets should queue requests so that no more than maxSockets are dispatched concurrently per host:port:path key. With maxSockets: 10 and 200 parallel http.request calls, the server should never see more than 10 in-flight.
What do you see instead?
Bun dispatches all 200 requests immediately; the server sees a peak of 200 concurrent in-flight requests. The Agent instance's maxSockets option is ignored (agent.sockets[origin] never grows past 0).
