Expected
Bun.WebView.closeAll() should terminate the Chrome browser and all its helpers (renderer, GPU, network, utility, crashpad). The docs say "browser subprocesses never outlive your script".
Actual
Only the main browser PID is killed. Helpers get reparented to PID 1 and never exit. In a long-running process they accumulate every time closeAll() runs.
Root cause
ChromeProcess.zig:

Spawn uses bun.spawn.spawnProcess with no setpgid/setsid — Chrome inherits Bun's group.
Bun__Chrome__kill() is process.kill(9) on the browser PID only — no killpg.
Lifetime coupling is --remote-debugging-pipe EOF, which only the browser is connected to; helpers can't detect it.

Chromium helpers on Linux only get PR_SET_PDEATHSIG if the launcher opts into kill_on_parent_death (launch_posix.cc), which most non-renderer helpers do not. --no-zygote is not the cause; GPU/network/utility/crashpad are direct browser children either way.
Proposed fix
Same pattern puppeteer/playwright/chrome-launcher use:

setpgid(0, 0) in the child at spawn (Chrome becomes its own process-group leader).
killpg(pgid, SIGTERM) → brief wait → killpg(pgid, SIGKILL) in Bun__Chrome__kill.

