status: 200

$ bun repro.js
error: ECONNREFUSED
```

### What is the expected behavior?

`closeAllConnections()` only closes established HTTP(S) connections; the listening socket stays open and new connections succeed (matching Node).

### What do you see instead?

The listener is destroyed too. Any follow-up GET to the same port gets `ECONNREFUSED`.

### Additional information

**Real-world impact.** Playwright's `TestServer.reset()` calls `_server.closeAllConnections()` between tests to drop straggling sockets, expecting the listener to stay up. Under Bun every test after the first sees `ECONNREFUSED` on `goto`, so essentially the entire `tests/library/*` and `tests/page/*` suites fail to run.

**Root cause.** `Server.prototype.closeAllConnections` in `src/js/node/_http_server.ts` calls `server.stop(true)`, which goes through `stop_listening` and tears down the listening socket. The wrapper also clears `serverSymbol`, `kConnectionsCheckingInterval`, and `listening` — none of which `closeAllConnections` is documented to do; those belong to `close()`.

