# 🐛 Bug Report: Unsound `Send` impls — generic `Context`/`T` lacks required bounds

## What version of Bun is running?

`1.3.14+0d9b296af` (analysis based on commit [`2148214d40`](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/commit/2148214d40fc9f844f61ae5f8575d6d94a9d038c))

## What platform is your computer?

`Linux 7.0.9-arch1-2-lily x86_64 unknown` — but the bug is platform-independent (it is a type-level soundness issue in the Rust workspace).

## What steps can reproduce the bug?

Found by static analysis. The unconditional `unsafe impl Send` for generic wrappers around heap-owned context lets safe code construct values that must not actually be `Send` and ship them across threads, violating the standard Rust aliasing model.

### Affected types

#### 1. `JsCell<T>` — both `Send` and `Sync` are unconditional, **`get(&self) -> &T` is safe**

[`src/jsc/JSCell.rs#L117-L142`](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/2148214d40fc9f844f61ae5f8575d6d94a9d038c/src/jsc/JSCell.rs#L117-L142)

```rust
#[repr(transparent)]
pub struct JsCell<T>(core::cell::UnsafeCell<T>);

unsafe impl<T> Sync for JsCell<T> {}   // ← no `T: Sync` bound
unsafe impl<T> Send for JsCell<T> {}   // ← no `T: Send` bound

impl<T> JsCell<T> {
    pub fn get(&self) -> &T {                   // ← SAFE function
        unsafe { &*self.0.get() }
    }
    // …
}
```

Combined with `Sync`, a `&'static JsCell<T>` is `Send`able. The **safe** `get()` then hands out a `&T` on the receiving thread. If `T` is `!Sync` (e.g. `Cell<U>`, `Rc<U>`, `RefCell<U>`), this is UB.

The single-JS-thread invariant is a runtime contract, not enforced by the type signature. Anyone who later writes `JsCell<Rc<Foo>>` — directly, or transitively through a struct field — breaks the model with **no `unsafe`** at the call site.

#### 2. `ConcurrentPromiseTask<'_, C>` — `Send` without `C: Send`

[`src/jsc/ConcurrentPromiseTask.rs#L31-L55`](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/2148214d40fc9f844f61ae5f8575d6d94a9d038c/src/jsc/ConcurrentPromiseTask.rs#L31-L55)

```rust
pub struct ConcurrentPromiseTask<'a, Context: ConcurrentPromiseTaskContext> {
    pub ctx: Box<Context>,                      // ← owned heap value
    // …
}

unsafe impl<C: ConcurrentPromiseTaskContext> Send for ConcurrentPromiseTask<'_, C> {}
//                                          ^^^^ no `C: Send`
```

`ctx: Box<Context>` is owned by value. The task is shipped to the work pool and dereferenced on a worker thread:

[`src/jsc/ConcurrentPromiseTask.rs#L84-L95`](https://github.

