### What does the bug do?

When a class contains any decorated member, standard decorator lowering rewrites private member accesses to `__privateGet`/`__privateMethod` WeakMap helpers. Optional chains that pass through such a lowered private access lose their short-circuiting: the nullish check from `?.` is not carried into the rewritten expression, so the helper is called with `undefined` and throws instead of the whole chain evaluating to `undefined`.

### Repro

```js
