### What does the bug do?

Split out of #31917 while fixing the inner-class-name / `this` substitution there. These two problems are specific to the accessor-only lowering path: a class that contains `accessor` members but no decorators. (When any member is decorated, all private members get WeakMap-lowered and the first problem does not reproduce.)

**1. Native private names in relocated static initializers / static blocks**

`lower_decorators.rs` extracts static blocks and relocates undecorated static `accessor` initializers into the module-level suffix chain. In the accessor-only case, private members are not WeakMap-lowered (`lower_all_private` is false), so the relocated code still contains native `#name` references, now outside any class body:

```js
const C = class Foo {
  static #m = function (tag) { return { tag }; };
  static accessor a = Foo.#m("a").tag;
};
console.log(C.a);
// SyntaxError: Cannot reference undeclared private names: "#m"
```

Same failure through a static block:

```js
const C = class Foo {
  static accessor a = 1;
  static #m = 5;
  static { console.log(this.#m); }
};
// SyntaxError: Cannot reference undeclared private names: "#m"
```

**2. Evaluation order of accessor initializers vs. static blocks**

Undecorated static accessor initializers are pushed into the suffix chain during the property loop, before extracted static blocks are appended, so relative source order is lost:

```js
const order = [];
const C = class {
  static accessor a = (order.push("a"), 1);
  static { order.push("block"); }
  static accessor b = (order.push("b"), 2);
};
console.log(order.join(","));
// bun:             a,b,block
// esbuild + spec:  a,block,b
```

esbuild avoids both problems by keeping the initializer inside the class for this case (a `static #a = init` backing field plus getter/setter) instead of relocating it. Fixing this likely means not relocating static elements at all when the class has no decorators, or forcing private lowering when relocation is unavoidable.

