## What is the issue?

`Subprocess.resourceUsage().cpuTime.user` and `cpuTime.system` return `bigint` instead of `number` as declared in the TypeScript type `ResourceUsage`. This causes `JSON.stringify()` to throw `TypeError: JSON.stringify cannot serialize BigInt.`

## How can we reproduce the crash?

```bash
bun -e "
const proc = Bun.spawn(['echo', 'test']);
await proc.exited;
const u = proc.resourceUsage?.();
if (u) {
  console.log('cpuTime.user type:', typeof u.cpuTime.user, 'value:', u.cpuTime.user);
  console.log('cpuTime.system type:', typeof u.cpuTime.system, 'value:', u.cpuTime.system);
  const metrics = { cpuTimeUser: u.cpuTime.user, cpuTimeSystem: u.cpuTime.system };
  try { JSON.stringify(metrics); console.log('JSON.stringify: OK'); } catch(e) { console.log('JSON.stringify ERROR:', e.message); }
}
"
```

