### What steps can reproduce the bug?

When a `Bun.serve` handler returns `new Response(stream)` where `stream` is a
`ReadableStream`, Bun pulls/enqueues from that stream as fast as it can, ignoring
whether the TCP socket can accept the data. If the client reads the body slowly or
stops reading, Bun buffers the entire body in memory.

Self-contained repro (safe — capped at 1 GiB so it won't OOM the box). Save as
`repro.mjs` and run `bun repro.mjs`:

```js
