`Buffer.byteLength(str, "utf8")` counts an unpaired surrogate as 2 bytes. Everything else in Bun encodes it as U+FFFD, which is 3 bytes. The gap surfaces as a short `Content-Length` and a truncated response body.

Unpaired surrogates are easy to produce by accident. Slicing a string at a character count can cut an emoji in half:

