## What happens

Replaying a recorded sequence of `CSSStyleDeclaration` calls against
`cssstyle@6.2.0` deterministically enters an infinite loop after ~197,000
calls. The loop is synchronous — pending timers never fire again — and it
allocates as it spins, so memory grows until the process is OOM-killed.
Because the event loop is blocked, a process that gets externally killed
mid-loop can also *appear* to exit silently, which is how this first showed up
(a long test-suite run that "exited 0" having written nothing).

The same script and data complete in a few seconds with the FTL tier disabled.

