### What steps can reproduce the bug?

`Bun.Image` (decode/resize/encode) allocates macOS `IOAccelerator`-tagged VM regions in **exactly 128 MB chunks**, sized to the **peak number of concurrent** `Bun.Image` operations, and this high-water mark is **never released for the lifetime of the process** — even after concurrency drops back to 1, even after `Bun.gc(true)`, even after long idle periods.

This is a different mechanism from #28234 (bmalloc/libpas arenas driven by Ink/React render-loop allocation churn, no GPU frameworks involved). Here the growth is driven purely by `Bun.Image` concurrency, is exactly reproducible, and scales far larger in practice (tens of GB, see Real-world impact below).

