### What steps can reproduce the bug?

A child that sends an IPC message and then exits loses the message when Bun is using the waiter-thread process-exit fallback (`BUN_FEATURE_FLAG_FORCE_WAITER_THREAD=1`, which is also the path taken when a pidfd cannot be used) and the parent gets to its event loop only after the child has already exited.

`ipc-lost.ts`:

```ts
let delivered = 0, lost = 0;
for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
  const { promise, resolve } = Promise.withResolvers();
  const a = Bun.spawn({
    cmd: [process.execPath, "-e", `process.send("hello"); Promise.resolve().then(() => process.exit(0));`],
    ipc: resolve,
    stdio: ["inherit", "inherit", "inherit"],
  });
  const b = Bun.spawn({
    cmd: [process.execPath, "-e", `Promise.resolve().then(() => { process.disconnect(); process.exit(0); });`],
    ipc() {},
    stdio: ["inherit", "inherit", "inherit"],
  });
  // Anything that keeps the parent off its event loop until after `a` has written and exited.
  Bun.spawnSync({ cmd: [process.execPath, "-e", "0"] });
  (await Promise.race([promise, Bun.sleep(3000).then(() => "TIMEOUT")])) === "hello" ? delivered++ : lost++;
  await Promise.all([a.exited, b.exited]);
}
console.log({ delivered, lost });
```

