### Summary

On macOS, `fs.watch` on a directory delivers about one event per 40ms no matter how many files actually changed. Writing 20 files in a tight loop produces 2 callbacks. Node produces 20.

The missing events are not delayed or merged into a later callback, they never arrive. The watcher keeps working afterwards, so nothing looks broken from the outside.

### Reproduction

`watch-burst.mjs` writes 20 files into a watched temp directory and counts how many of them the watcher reported, repeated for five write spacings. No dependencies.

```js
