### What is the expected behavior?

Balanced output: 7 `<strong>` and 7 `</strong>` in the first case (every consumed delimiter character corresponds to an emitted tag), and either 7 nested pairs or literal asterisks for the unconsumed characters in the second case. md4c prints 7 nested pairs in both cases.

### What do you see instead?

Unbalanced HTML in the first case (`<strong>` x6, `</strong>` x7) and silently dropped characters in the second.

Cause: `EmphDelim` in src/md/inlines.rs records the individual match sizes of a delimiter run in `open_sizes` / `close_sizes`, fixed arrays of `MAX_EMPH_MATCHES` (6) entries. `resolve_emphasis_delimiters` keeps consuming characters past the sixth match (`open_count` / `close_count` still grow, so the characters are not printed as text), but `emit_emph_open_tags` / `emit_emph_close_tags` only see the recorded sizes. The opener and each closer truncate independently, which is what makes the one-opener-many-closers case unbalanced rather than merely lossy.

The `underline` option (#39493) is not affected: it emits one `<u>` per consumed character straight from the counts, so it does not go through the size arrays.

