### Additional information

This is not a theoretical compatibility gap — it silently disables a Next.js feature.

Next.js ships a filter (`next/dist/server/node-environment-extensions/unhandled-rejection.external.js`) whose job is to suppress the expected rejections produced when a prerender is aborted — the ones you get from late-awaited data in a render that got cancelled. With `cacheComponents` and `partialPrefetching` enabled, cancelled prefetches produce these constantly.

The filter's entire suppression decision is this:

```js
