export const a: ReturnType<Event["composedPath"]> = path;
```

```
error TS2322: Type 'EventTarget[]' is not assignable to type '[(EventTarget | undefined)?]'.
  Target allows only 1 element(s) but source may have more.
```

The tuple is correct for Node's minimal `Event` (its own doc comment says "not used in Node.js"), but it is wrong for the DOM, where `composedPath()` returns the full propagation path. Any DOM implementation typed against lib.dom becomes unassignable to `Event`, and that propagates: every `EventTarget` is affected, so `Node`, `Element` and `Document` all fail too.

`globals.d.ts` already has the mechanism to avoid this — `TextDecoder` and others are declared through `Bun.__internal.UseLibDomIfAvailable<…>` / `LibDomIsLoaded`, which appears 24 times in that file. `Event` (line 272) and `EventTarget` (line 341) are declared as bare interfaces instead, so they merge rather than defer.

