### What steps can reproduce the bug?

`node:http` and `node:https` export the same `Server` constructor, so every
plain HTTP server passes an `instanceof https.Server` check:

```js
import http from 'node:http';
import https from 'node:https';

console.log(http.Server === https.Server);                     // bun: true   node: false
console.log(http.createServer() instanceof https.Server);      // bun: true   node: false
```

This is not just cosmetic. Distinguishing HTTP from HTTPS is how libraries pick
between the `'connection'` and `'secureConnection'` events, because for a TLS
server the socket that becomes `req.socket` is the one from
`'secureConnection'`. On Bun that discrimination silently selects the wrong
event, so per-socket cleanup is registered on an event that never fires and the
library leaks a socket per connection.

`@apollo/server`'s `ApolloServerPluginDrainHttpServer` does exactly this
([`stoppable.ts`](https://github.com/apollographql/apollo-server/blob/main/packages/server/src/plugin/drainHttpServer/stoppable.ts)):

```js
