### Why

- In node `socket.bytesRead` reads a native counter on the handle. The handle adds to it on each read, whatever consumes the bytes.
- In bun `bytesRead` is a plain property on the `net.Socket`. Only the JS `data` handlers in `src/js/node/net.ts` add to it.
