## Summary

With Bun 1.4.2 and MySQL 8.4.5, `SQL.unsafe()` can keep rejecting a prepared SELECT after its initial missing-table error, even after that table has been created on the same connection pool. A SELECT with different SQL text succeeds immediately.

Found while testing https://github.com/stacksjs/stacks/issues/2623. CI on Linux also fails the same auth-owner regression cases; the minimal reproduction below was verified on macOS arm64. This affects optional-schema readers that tolerate an absent table and expect a later installation to become visible without restarting the process.

## Reproduction

Run against a disposable local MySQL database. The table name below must not already exist.

```ts
import { SQL } from 'bun'

const sql = new SQL(process.env.TEST_MYSQL_URL!)
const query = 'SELECT password_changed_at FROM prepare_probe WHERE id = ? LIMIT 1'
try {
  try { await sql.unsafe(query, [42]) }
  catch (error) { console.log('expected missing table:', error) }

  await sql.unsafe('CREATE TABLE prepare_probe (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, password_changed_at TIMESTAMP)')
  await sql.unsafe("INSERT INTO prepare_probe VALUES (42, '2026-09-15 10:00:00')")

  try { console.log('same query:', await sql.unsafe(query, [42])) }
  catch (error) { console.log('unexpected rejection:', error) }

  console.log('different text:', await sql.unsafe(`${query} `, [42]))
}
finally {
  await sql.unsafe('DROP TABLE IF EXISTS prepare_probe')
  await sql.close()
}
```

Expected: both SELECTs after CREATE/INSERT return the row.

Actual: the original SELECT rejects again; the same SELECT with one trailing space returns the row. Changing query text is diagnostic evidence only, not a proposed application fix.

Version: `bun 1.4.2 (744846f84)`, MySQL 8.4.5, macOS arm64. Stacks CI failure: https://github.com/stacksjs/stacks/actions/runs/34850416526.

