`url.domainToUnicode` takes time that grows with the square of the number of `xn--` labels in the host. The review of #42856 measured it. #42856 does not change it, and `main` does the same.

### Reproduction

```js
import url from "node:url";

for (const n of [4096, 8192, 16384, 32768]) {
  const host = "xn--nxa.".repeat(n) + "com";
  const start = performance.now();
  url.domainToUnicode(host);
  console.log(n, "labels:", (performance.now() - start).toFixed(0), "ms");
}
```

| Labels | Host length | Bun (release build of 7e56b402b, linux x64) | Node 26.3.0 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 4096 | 32 KB | 78 ms | 2 ms |
| 8192 | 64 KB | 315 ms | 2 ms |
| 16384 | 128 KB | 1252 ms | 4 ms |
| 32768 | 256 KB | 5032 ms | 7 ms |

### Cause

- `icuToUnicode` (`src/jsc/bindings/NodeURL.cpp`) calls `uidna_nameToUnicode` on the whole host.
- ICU decodes each label in place. `UTS46::processLabel` calls `replaceLabel`, which calls `UnicodeString::replace` on the whole name. That call moves the rest of the name for each decoded label.
- The other paths are linear. `url.domainToASCII`, `new URL` and the ICU check in `hasValidPunycodeHost` take 16 ms for the 32768-label host with a right-to-left label in front, because ToASCII leaves a valid punycode label as it is.

### Possible fix

Convert label by label in `jsDomainToUnicode`: split the parsed host at `.`, give each `xn--` label to `uidna_labelToUnicode`, and copy the other labels. The parsed host is lowercase ASCII at that point, so the mapping and normalization steps of the whole-name conversion change nothing. A differential test against `uidna_nameToUnicode` must show that the output is the same.

