### What happens

On Windows, a process that runs under `bun --watch` does not get the IPC channel that its parent gave it. `process.send` exists in the child, but a message never reaches the other side, in either direction. No error is printed.

### Repro

`parent.js`:

```js
const { fork } = require("node:child_process");
const child = fork(__dirname + "/child.js", { execArgv: ["--watch"] });
child.on("message", message => {
  console.log("parent got", message);
  child.kill();
});
setTimeout(() => {
  console.log("parent: no message after 5 s");
  child.kill();
}, 5000).unref();
```

`child.js`:

```js
