### Additional information

The cause is the order of the checks in `Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/StringPrototype.cpp` (oven-sh/WebKit `c28156899e`, and upstream WebKit `main`):

- `stringProtoFuncReplace` and `stringProtoFuncReplaceAll` check `RegExpObject::isSymbolReplaceFastAndNonObservable()`, convert `this`, check again, and call the 5-argument `replaceUsingRegExpSearch()`.
- That overload converts `replaceValue` with `toWTFString()` and continues on the fast path. Nothing checks the RegExp after that conversion.
- The same holds when the `toString` replaces `RegExp.prototype.exec`, sets `re.lastIndex` to an object, or defines an own `flags`.
- `replace<>()` in `StringPrototypeInlines.h`, behind `operationStringProtoFuncReplaceGeneric`, calls the same overload after `ToString(this)` with no check at all.

`JSTests/stress/string-replace-regexp-fast-path-tostring-side-effects.js` covers the conversion of `this` in the host function. No test covers the conversion of `replaceValue`.

A direct call, `re[Symbol.replace]("aaa", replaceValue)`, prints `aaa 1`. oven-sh/WebKit#682 gives the direct call the same fast path and converts `replaceValue` before the check, so it keeps that result. It does not change the String side. A fix belongs in the 5-argument overload, with tests for the host function and for the DFG operation.

