### Cause

1. libuv maps every inotify mask bit outside `IN_ATTRIB|IN_MODIFY` to `UV_RENAME` ([linux.c#L2611-L2615](https://github.com/libuv/libuv/blob/v1.52.1/src/unix/linux.c#L2611-L2615)). For a directory the kernel also sets `IN_ISDIR`, so the event has both `UV_CHANGE` and `UV_RENAME`, and Node prefers `rename`. The inotify dispatch in `src/runtime/node/path_watcher.rs` reports `rename` only for the create, delete and move bits.
2. libuv reports `uv__basename_r(path)`, the bytes after the last `/` of the path as the caller gave it ([linux.c#L2625](https://github.com/libuv/libuv/blob/v1.52.1/src/unix/linux.c#L2625)). `FSWatcher::init` joins the path with the cwd and normalizes it before it reaches `path_watcher::watch`

