`completeUpgrade()` in `src/js/thirdparty/ws.js` does not use `head`. It gives the connection to the native WebSocket with `server.upgrade()`. The npm package calls `socket.unshift(head)` and reads frames from the socket stream, so it parses every byte that arrived before the upgrade.

In the first three rows the early frames are in the `head` argument of the 'upgrade' event. In the last row they reach the `net.Socket` of the 'upgrade' event as data. The shim has no way to give either to the native WebSocket parser.

