In the code below, the server writes a 32MiB response while the client stalls reading for 250ms. That exceeds what kernel socket buffers can absorb (~11 MiB on loopback), so at `res.end()` time a large backlog is still buffered in userspace.

`node`: `cb` fires ~250ms later once the backlog drains (`PASS`)
