### Additional information

A `Query` is lazy. It runs when it is awaited or when `.execute()` is called. The handle state (`closed`, `acceptQueries`) is read when the query is created. `queryFromTransactionHandler` in `src/js/bun/sql.ts` runs the query on the connection that was captured at creation and does not read the state again. So a query that is created while the handle is open and first awaited after the handle closed still runs.

