### What happens

Bun converts an `encoding` argument that is not a string in a different way than Node. Node's `getEncodingOps` ([`lib/buffer.js`](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v26.3.0/lib/buffer.js#L790-L791)) does `encoding += ''`. That is `ToPrimitive` with the default hint, so `valueOf()` runs before `toString()`.

- `Buffer.byteLength(string, encoding)` ignores every encoding that is not a string primitive (`jsBufferConstructorFunction_byteLengthBody` in `src/jsc/bindings/JSBuffer.cpp`).
- `parseEncoding` in the same file calls `toString()` on the value first. `buf.toString`, `buf.write` and `buf.indexOf` use it.

