### What happens

A macro that uses a `FinalizationRegistry` can leave the event loop of a `Bun.build()` worker thread active for the rest of the process. The cleanup job of the registry never runs on that thread.

This has no visible effect today. Nothing reads the active count of a bundler worker's loop. It matters for #40769: its idle check for a macro promise that never settles reads that count, so a later build on the same thread hangs and does not report the error.

