On a `node:http2` server, `stream.end()` (or `stream.end(data)`) followed by `stream.pushStream()` in the same tick writes the PUSH_PROMISE after the END_STREAM of the parent stream. RFC 9113 section 6.6 allows a PUSH_PROMISE only on a stream that is "open" or "half-closed (remote)" for the sender. A node client cancels that push: the pushed stream closes on the server with `rstCode` 8 and the client never emits the session `'stream'` event.

Frame order that a raw TCP client sees for one GET (bun 1.4.3-canary.1+367d939d9 and main at 26e7a4b369, node v26.3.0):

```
