In `src/js/node/http2.ts`, the `pushAllowed` getter of the server stream has no `session.closed` term, and `pushStream` checks only `session.destroyed` and `pushAllowed`. `ServerHttp2Session.ping` and the `ping` of the client session have no `closed` or `connecting` short-circuit. A pushed stream that opens after `close()` also goes through `streamStart`, which adds to the open-stream count of the closed session.

