### What happens

Two requests arrive pipelined on one connection. The `'request'` listener destroys the second response while it is still queued behind the first one. The second request then never emits `'aborted'`, `'error'` or `'close'`. A consumer that waits for the end of that request (`for await`, `stream.finished`, a body parser) never settles.

