### What happens

A worker creates an inner `Worker` and transfers a `FileHandle` to it through `workerData` and `transferList`. The outer worker then exits (`process.exit()`), or its parent terminates it, before the inner worker unpacks its `workerData`. The fd stays open for the life of the process. Node closes it.

#43541 closes the fd when the thread that made the Worker is still alive at the exit of that Worker. This issue is the case that #43541 cannot cover. The `close` event of the inner Worker never reaches the outer thread, and no JS runs on that thread any more.

