### Cause

`Http2Stream.end()` in `src/js/node/http2.ts` keeps a `StreamState.EndedCalled` bit. When the bit is set it calls the callback and returns, and it never reaches `super.end(chunk, encoding, callback)`. Node's `Writable.prototype.end` calls `_write()` for a chunk that is not null, and `_write()` on an ending stream creates `ERR_STREAM_WRITE_AFTER_END`, passes it to the callback and calls `errorOrDestroy`.

