```

| | polyfill (bun 1.4.3) | `node entry.js` and `bun entry.js` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | `-1 -1 false` | `0 6 true` |
| 2 | `val must be string, number or Buffer` | `1` |
| 3 | `2 5` | `-1 2` |

### Cause

All three are in `bidirectionalIndexOf` in `src/node-fallbacks/buffer.js`.

- An empty value: `if (val.length === 0) return -1`, and the `buffer.length === 0` return at the top of the function. Node.js returns the clamped offset ([`IndexOfString`](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v26.3.0/src/node_buffer.cc#L1007-L1013)).
- A `Uint8Array` value: the check is `Buffer.isBuffer(val)`. Node.js uses `isUint8Array(val)`.
- The `end` argument: the methods take `(val, byteOffset, encoding)`. Node.js v26 takes `(val, byteOffset, end, encoding)` ([`lib/buffer.js`](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v26.3.0/lib/buffer.js#L1089-L1097)).

The errors that these methods throw also have no `code` (`ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE`, `ERR_UNKNOWN_ENCODING`).

Upstream `feross/buffer` behaves the same way. #43654 changes the offset and UTF-16 handling of the same functions. It does not change these forms.

