### Additional information

The cause is in `src/js/thirdparty/ws.js`. The request that `finishRequest` gets keeps a copy of `options.headers` with the names as the caller wrote them (line 227). `setHeader()`, `getHeader()`, `hasHeader()` and `removeHeader()` use the name in lowercase (lines 236 to 251). A name with an uppercase letter thus has two keys, and the native `WebSocket` joins the two values.

The effects:

| Call | Node + `ws` 8.18.3 | Bun |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `req.getHeader("X-Token")` before `setHeader()` | `"a"` | `undefined` |
| `req.hasHeader("X-Token")` before `setHeader()` | `true` | `false` |
| `req.setHeader("X-Token", "b")` | the server gets `X-Token: b` | the server gets `X-Token: a, b` |
| `req.removeHeader("X-Token")` | the header is not sent | the server gets `X-Token: a` |
| `req.getHeaders()` after `setHeader()` | one key, `x-token` | two keys, `X-Token` and `x-token` |

A header that `options.headers` names in lowercase is not affected.

