A recursive `fs.watch()` on Linux walks the tree and adds one inotify watch for each directory. The walk runs when the watch starts, and again when a directory appears in the watched tree. When the walk cannot open or read a directory, it skips everything below that directory and reports nothing. The watcher stays open and looks healthy. Events from the skipped part never arrive.

No user reported this. It came up during work on the walk itself.

### Reproduction

