User code in these listeners can change what the rest of the chunk does. One case from #43465: `req.destroy()` in the `'response'` listener, with a PUSH_PROMISE on that request later in the same chunk. In node the listener runs after the PUSH_PROMISE was accepted, so the session emits `'stream'`. In Bun the listener runs first. Before #43465 Bun surfaces the push like node. With #43465 Bun cancels it (RST_STREAM(CANCEL)), because the request is already destroyed when the frame is parsed. On a socket both runtimes cancel it.

