### 1. One parser error stands for several llhttp errors

The uWS parser (`packages/bun-uws/src/HttpParser.h`) reports a class of failure as one `HttpParserError` value. `onServerClientError` (`src/js/node/_http_server.ts`) maps that value to one code and one text. llhttp reports the exact rule. So for six arms (chunk size, transfer-encoding, request line, method, version, header token) the text is right for the most common input and wrong for the others. These arms have no `err.reason`, because no single reason is right.

Same code, other reason (the `HPE_` prefix is left out):

| Bad request | node v26.3.0 reason | Bun message |
|---|---|---|
| chunk size `FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF` | Chunk size overflow | Parse Error: Invalid character in chunk size |
| `Transfer-Encoding: chunked, gzip`, or `chunked` in two fields | Invalid \`Transfer-Encoding\` header value | Parse Error: Request has invalid \`Transfer-Encoding\` |
| `Content-Length: 5`, then `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` | Transfer-Encoding can't be present with Content-Length | Parse Error: Request has invalid \`Transfer-Encoding\` |
| `GET / HTTP/1.1 x`, `GET / HTTP/1.10`, or a bare LF after the version | Expected CRLF after version |

