## What happens

On macOS, `fs.realpathSync`, `fs.realpathSync.native`, and `fs.promises.realpath` throw `EPERM` for a cloud-storage directory under `~/Library/CloudStorage` (a File Provider domain), and for a symlink that points at one. Node 24 resolves the same paths. In the same Bun process, `lstatSync`, `statSync`, `accessSync`, and `existsSync` succeed on the path, so the entry is reachable and only `realpath` fails.

Reproduced with File Provider directories from two different cloud-storage providers. On this machine `readdirSync` on those directories also fails with `EPERM (scandir)` under both runtimes, because macOS privacy controls protect them. Node's `realpath` succeeds anyway.

## Environment

- macOS (Darwin 27.0.0, Apple Silicon)
- Bun 1.3.14 (`bun --revision`: `1.3.14+0d9b296af`) and Bun 1.4.2 (`bunx bun@latest`), both reproduce
- Node v24.21.0, does not reproduce
- Directory: `~/Library/CloudStorage/<Provider>-<Account>`, mode `drwx------@`, with the xattr `com.apple.file-provider-domain-id`
- Symlink: `~/<Provider> -> ~/Library/CloudStorage/<Provider>-<Account>`, as the provider apps create it

