### What happens

A raw QUIC `node:quic` client creates a unidirectional stream before its handshake ends. The stream never opens. `stream.pending` stays `true`, `stream.id` stays `null`, and the body never reaches the server. A bidirectional stream in the same place opens when the handshake ends.

Node v26.3.0 (built with QUIC, run with `--experimental-quic`) opens the stream after the handshake and delivers the body.

