**Bun version:** 1.3.14 (macOS arm64)

### What happens
When a matcher fails, `toBe` / `toBeNull` format the received value through
`Symbol.for("nodejs.util.inspect.custom")`, but the diff-producing matchers
(`toEqual`, `toStrictEqual`, `toMatchObject`, `toHaveBeenCalledWith` and friends)
do not. They walk and print every own property (including non-enumerable and
symbol keys), so a value with a large reachable graph produces a multi-megabyte
failure message. With DOM test environments (happy-dom) a single node reaches the
window, document and framework internals; inside a retrying `waitFor` this
exhausts memory before the retry can time out. Snapshot serialisation has the
same behaviour, and `expect.addSnapshotSerializer` throws "Not implemented", so
there is no supported way to bound the output.

### Reproduction
```ts
