### What happens

Node.js documents two `QuicStream` members that Bun does not implement:

- [`stream.opened`](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v26.11.1/doc/api/quic.md#streamopened) (added in v26.10.0): a promise fulfilled when a stream created without stream credit is opened and gets its ID. In Bun it is `undefined`, so an application must poll `stream.pending` to learn when the stream can be used.
- [`stream.onstopsending`](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v26.11.1/doc/api/quic.md#streamonstopsending) (added in v26.7.0): called when the peer sends STOP_SENDING. In Bun, setting it has no effect and the only observable change is that `writer.desiredSize` becomes `null`, so an application must poll the writer to learn that the peer stopped reading.

