### Additional information

After the client's session is gone, Bun emits `'drain'` on the server stream, drops the buffered data and keeps returning `true` from `write()`; `'aborted'`/`'close'` only arrive after the handler returns. If the client only sends RST_STREAM (`req.close(NGHTTP2_CANCEL)`) and keeps its session, Bun closes the stream like Node. Upstream report of the same scenario: nodejs/node#18973.

