The declarations are `udp.SocketHandler` and `udp.ConnectedSocketHandler`:
https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/91e7e3b140eaef348b7bc33d564dcb67b7de4ddd/packages/bun-types/bun.d.ts#L7551
https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/91e7e3b140eaef348b7bc33d564dcb67b7de4ddd/packages/bun-types/bun.d.ts#L7563

The runtime passes only the error:
https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/91e7e3b140eaef348b7bc33d564dcb67b7de4ddd/src/runtime/socket/udp_socket.rs#L867-L873

`node:dgram` already relies on the one-argument form (`error: error => ...`), so changing the types looks safer than changing the runtime:

```ts
error?(this: Socket<DataBinaryType>, error: Error): void | Promise<void>;
error?(this: ConnectedSocket<DataBinaryType>, error: Error): void | Promise<void>;
```

