### What happens

Under parallel load, `child_process.spawnSync` (and `execFileSync`, which uses it) sometimes returns `stdout === ""` for a child that printed output and exited 0. `status` is `0`, `signal` is `null`, `error` is `undefined`, so nothing tells the caller that output was lost.

Node 22 never does this on the same machine and load. In Bun, the async APIs (`child_process.spawn`, `Bun.spawn`) never do it, and neither does `spawnSync` when stdout goes to a file descriptor instead of a pipe.

### Repro

`probe.ts`:

```ts
import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';
import { closeSync, mkdtempSync, openSync, readFileSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
import { join } from 'node:path';

const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'probe-'));
const f = join(dir, 'in.txt');
writeFileSync(f, '# Next Up\n\n## Fix transform sync drift\n\n- Reproduce\n- Patch\n- Validate\n');
const want = readFileSync(f, 'utf8');

let pipeBad = 0;
let fileBad = 0;
let example = '';
for (let i = 0; i < 300; i++) {
  const r = spawnSync('cat', [f], { encoding: 'utf8' });
  if (r.stdout !== want) {
    pipeBad++;
    example = `status=${r.status} signal=${r.signal} error=${r.error} stdout.length=${r.stdout?.length}`;
  }
  const out = join(dir, `o${i}`);
  const fd = openSync(out, 'w');
  spawnSync('cat', [f], { stdio: ['ignore', fd, 'pipe'] });
  closeSync(fd);
  if (readFileSync(out, 'utf8') !== want) fileBad++;
}
rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });
console.log(`pipe-bad=${pipeBad} file-bad=${fileBad} ${example}`);
```

