### Additional information

- Calling `res.destroy()` synchronously inside the handler closes the connection with no response on both runtimes; only a destroy after the handler returns sends the `200 OK`.
- `req.socket.destroy()` closes without a response on both runtimes, so it works as a workaround.
- Impact: a forward proxy that destroys the client response when its upstream request fails (e.g. `ECONNRESET`) makes the client see `200 OK` with an empty body instead of a network error. We hit this in a test-owned HTTP proxy that audits browser traffic: an upstream reset reached the browser as a success.

